RESOURCES/notes — what the literature is and why it matters here
================================================================

Bib keys match ../DOC/paper.bib (via additional.bib symlink). Each cited
work should have a matching <key>.pdf in this directory.

Central to the method
---------------------

patnaik2021but
  The source of the cloud-bias correction. Shows that VIIRS monthly
  composites are biased downward in cloudy months because cloud-free
  observations are non-randomly missing, and derives the correction that
  NighttimeLights.jl implements as bias_PSTT2021 / the PSTT2021 pipeline.
  This is the paper the software is the reference implementation of.

uprety2019calibration
  VIIRS DNB v2 reprocessing / calibration. Establishes the stray-light
  ("sl") corrected product that the replication downloads and cleans.

guptaEtal2017_analysisViirsDerivedNightlightOverIndia
  VIIRS-DNB behaviour over India specifically; motivates outlier and
  background-noise handling for the Indian context used in the example.

pearson2002outliers
  Outlier detection in process data; background for the Hampel-filter
  outlier step (outlier_hampel).

Economic-activity motivation
----------------------------

doll2006mapping
  Early demonstration that night-light radiance maps regional economic
  activity. Part of the "why night lights" case in the Summary.

hendersonEtal2012_measuringEconomicGrowthFromOuterSpace
  Canonical economics reference: night lights as a proxy for GDP growth
  where official statistics are weak.

donaldsonEtal2016_viewFromAboveApplicationSatelliteDataEconomics
  Survey of satellite data in economics; frames night lights as alternative
  data.

gibson2020night
  Critical review of night-lights sources and their pitfalls in economics —
  supports the "not analysis-ready" argument for a cleaning package.

State of the field / comparison tools
-------------------------------------

elvidge2013viirs        VIIRS superior to DMSP-OLS for night-lights mapping.
li2020harmonized        Harmonised DMSP+VIIRS 1992-2018 series.
marty2024blackmarbler    R package: downloads NASA Black Marble, zonal stats.
marty2024blackmarblepy   Python counterpart of blackmarbler.
njoku2019rnightlights    R package: DMSP-OLS / VIIRS extraction.
gorelick2017gee          Google Earth Engine — server-side access/aggregation.
  These four are the "existing tools" NighttimeLights.jl is distinguished
  from: they do acquisition and spatial aggregation, not statistical
  cleaning or cloud-bias correction.

Applications built on the package
---------------------------------

hande2025shedding        Wartime economic activity, Russia-Ukraine.
aviliani2026lights       Regional economic patterns, Java, Indonesia.
xkdr2026indiabuiltlit    Public India Built-and-Lit cleaned NL dataset.

